From 8fc0f03d7de55ab2c39367ecf24c187079523dd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Duy Truong <duytruong@google.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 05:45:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix OOB read and UAF in InputDispatcher::flushSensor

In `InputDispatcher::flushSensor()`, erasing an element from
`mInboundQueue` returns an iterator that was unconditionally incremented
by the loop. If the erased element was the last one, the increment
advanced the iterator past `end()`, resulting in an out-of-bounds read
and use-after-free when the next iteration dereferenced the invalid
iterator.

This patch fixes the issue by updating the loop to only increment the
iterator when an element is not erased. Additionally, the function now
properly inspects the `SensorEntry` fields to ensure only inbound sensor
events matching the specified `deviceId` and `sensorType` parameters are
erased, whereas previously it was unconditionally erasing all sensor
events.

This change also includes additional fix in tests to make them
deterministic by freeze dispatching before the events are enqueued, then
add the events, and then call flush.

Test: atest inputflinger_tests --host
Bug: 514737201
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX
Low-Coverage-Reason: coverage infra is broken

